== no foreign code: bounded, and unbounded by nothing
{
  "bounded": true,
  "unbounded_by": [],
ok the symbol list is empty
ok no UNBOUNDED
ok no unbounded-by section
ok it says it never touches foreign code
== one libc symbol is named exactly
{
  "bounded": false,
  "unbounded_by": [
    "libc:getpid"
  ],
  "effects": ["ffi"],
  "labels": [
    { "name": "ffi", "argument": "libc", "bounded": false }
  ],
  "never_touches": ["the console", "the filesystem", "the network", "the heap", "the command line", "signals", "other programs"],
  "foreign_symbols": ["getpid"],
  "pure": [],
  "functions": 2
}
UNBOUNDED: this program calls foreign code. The labels below bound it
everywhere except through the symbols under "unbounded by", and what
a symbol does is the linked library's, not the language's.
See docs/foreign-authority.md.
performs
    ffi("libc")    <- unbounded
never touches
    the console
    the filesystem
    the network
    the heap
    the command line
    signals
    other programs
unbounded by
    libc:getpid
exit 0
== two libraries are attributed symbol by symbol
{
  "bounded": false,
  "unbounded_by": [
    "libc:labs",
    "libpthread:pthread_self"
  ],
ok libc label
ok libpthread label
ok both symbols, sorted
unbounded by
    libc:labs
    libpthread:pthread_self
exit 7
